# c2c relay enable ignores ambient C2C_RELAY_URL and activates the public relay instead

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

c2c relay enable ignores an ambient C2C_RELAY_URL: chosen = match url with Some u -> u | _ -> default_public_relay_url (c2c_relay_cmd.ml:693-696). An operator with C2C_RELAY_URL=https://private.example exported who runs c2c relay enable gets the PUBLIC relay written to relay.json, and since machine_relay_config_has_url then holds, no Environment= pin is added - the systemd connector boots onto relay.c2c.im while the shell commands all used the private relay. Traffic silently splits across two relays. Env-over-config precedence is honored by every other activation surface (B300).

## Fix direction

chosen should fall back through Relay_activation.url () (flag > env > existing config) before the public default.

## Evidence

CLI review 2026-09-17; verified in source by coordinator.